# Generated artefacts. Everything here is rebuilt from a seed with the commands in
# README.md, so the repository holds no binaries and no large data files. LAYOUT.md
# explains each exclusion and gives the sizes, so the decision can be checked rather
# than trusted, and REGENERATED.md carries the SHA-256 of every excluded file.

# Messy Scan: rendered documents and render intermediates. 1.4 GB and 373 MB.
datasets/messy-scan/build/
datasets/messy-scan/documents/
datasets/messy-scan/sample/documents/

# Honest Containment: rendered audio. 79 MB. audio-manifest.jsonl carries the hashes.
datasets/honest-containment/audio/

# The private splits. Never published, at any size.
datasets/*/private/

# Working files a labeller produces. Labels are committed deliberately, not by accident.
datasets/honest-containment/labelling/packets/
datasets/honest-containment/labelling/labels-*.csv
datasets/honest-containment/labelling/judge-agreement.json

# The file a person fills with endpoints and key names. The example is committed instead.
datasets/honest-containment/suite/config/agents.json

# Large regenerable data files. Each is rebuilt from the seed by the script beside it, and
# its size and SHA-256 are in REGENERATED.md so a rebuild can be checked. LAYOUT.md 2.6 says
# why, and lists what is committed in their place: the generators, the manifests, a small
# sample/preview.jsonl per dataset, and the results pages themselves.
datasets/messy-scan/ground-truth.jsonl
datasets/messy-scan/sample/ground-truth.jsonl
datasets/exception-economics/ground-truth.jsonl
datasets/exception-economics/sample/ground-truth.jsonl
datasets/honest-containment/scenarios.jsonl
datasets/honest-containment/transcripts/
datasets/honest-containment/audio-specs.jsonl
datasets/honest-containment/audio-manifest.jsonl
results/exception-economics-v1.0/drift.json
results/exception-economics-v1.0/scores-baseline.json
results/exception-economics-v1.0/scores-all.json
results/honest-containment-v1.0/runs/*/run-*/contacts.jsonl
results/honest-containment-v1.0/runs/*/run-*/scored-contacts.jsonl

# manifest.json and MANIFEST.md are NOT ignored, in any dataset. They are small, they name
# every item with its hash, and a reader wants them without running a generator.

# Caches and build output
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
.DS_Store

# Anything that looks like a key, in case a local run writes one out
.env
.env.*
*.pem
